+## Searching orders
+
+The Orders page (`/orders/`) has a server-side search that is carried in the
+URL, so a search result can be bookmarked or shared. The search term is the
+`q` query parameter:
+
+- `/orders/?q=WS-2026` — orders whose order number contains `WS-2026`.
+- `/orders/?q=northside` — for staff, orders whose order number **or** account
+  name contains "northside".
+- `/orders/?status=pending&q=northside` — staff status and type filters combine
+  with the search; an order must match both.
+
+Matching ignores case and leading/trailing spaces, and the term is literal text
+(`%` and `_` are not wildcards). Customers only ever search their own orders, by
+order number. An empty `q` shows the usual list. The filter box above the table
+only narrows the rows already on the page and is not part of the URL.
+
 ## Using this for the Claude training exercises
 
 Three integration points, each independent of the others:
